name: Experimental source graphs preserve partial artifacts and never replace accepted Map context
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/cpg_module.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
submit: setup
require-live-snap: 30 SETUP · READY THE MAP RUN | setup-before-graph
expect-not: Map ✓
submit: run cpg:build {"languages":"go","subdir":"first","maxSourceFiles":2}
wait: 0.5
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 Source scope: first | scoped-graph-receipt
nav-mode:
keys: z
require-live-snap: 20 READ TRANSCRIPT | graph-reader
resize: 160x48
live-snap: graph-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: graph-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: graph-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: graph-60x20
resize: 40x12
keys: End
live-snap: graph-40x12-tail
keys: PPage
live-snap: graph-40x12-page-1
keys: PPage
live-snap: graph-40x12-page-2
keys: PPage
live-snap: graph-40x12-page-3
keys: PPage
live-snap: graph-40x12-page-4
ask: Are the selected first-directory scope, actual parsed counts, graph path, auxiliary Map role and unbounded collection limitations readable at all six sizes?
keys: q
resize: 120x36
submit: run cpg:build {"languages":"go,python","maxSourceFiles":2}
wait: 0.5
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 cpg:build partial | retained-first-language
expect: python
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/cpg_module.py @TMP_TARGET @ART partial
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/cpg_module.py @TMP_TARGET @ART changed
submit: run cpg:build {"languages":"go","maxSourceFiles":1}
wait: 0.5
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 cap of 1 | refused-stale-build
submit: run cpg:build {"languages":"go","maxSourceFiles":2}
wait: 0.5
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 Source scope: . | explicit-rebuild
submit: setup
require-live-snap: 25 SETUP · READY THE MAP RUN | setup-after-graphs
expect-not: Map ✓
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/cpg_module.py @TMP_TARGET @ART verified
ask: Does a later language failure retain the earlier graph in a partial receipt, with explicit file-cap refusal/rebuild and Map still awaiting context acceptance?
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 10 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT | explicit-quit
keys: y
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
submit: setup
require-live-snap: 30 SETUP · READY THE MAP RUN | restarted-setup
expect-not: Map ✓
submit: run cpg:build {"languages":"go","subdir":"first","maxSourceFiles":2}
wait: 0.5
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 Source scope: first | restarted-graph
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/cpg_module.py @TMP_TARGET @ART recovered
ask: Does no-color restart preserve graph artifacts and the partial failure without provider requests, findings, decisions or an accepted Map checkpoint?
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 10 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT | explicit-restart-quit
keys: y
require-exit: 10
